==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|thingum|y}}. Compare {{m|en|thingamabob}} and {{m|en|thingamajig}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈθɪŋəmi/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{syn of|en|thingy|nodot=a}}: [[something]] [[one]] [[cannot]] [[remember]] the [[name]] of, or is [[unable]] to or does not [[care]] to [[specify]] [[precisely]].
# {{syn of|en|whatshisname|nodot=a}}: [[someone]] [[one]] [[cannot]] [[remember]] the [[name]] of.
#* {{RQ:Fry Liar|pages=7–8|pageref=7|passage=Once, in his first term, Cartwright had been bold enough to ask him why he was so clever, {{...}}<br>‘It’s memory, Cartwright, old dear. Memory, the mother of the Muses .&nbsp;.&nbsp;. at least that’s what '''thingummy''' said.’<br>‘Who?’<br>‘You know, what’s his name, Greek poet chap. Wrote the {{w|Theogony}} .&nbsp;.&nbsp;. what ''was'' he called? Begins with an “H”.’<br>‘{{w|Homer}}?’<br>‘No, dear. Not Homer, the other one. No, it’s gone. Anyway. Memory, that’s the key.’}}

